<title>UZBEKISTAN: Uzbekistan swings into $231 mln Jan-Sept trade gap.</title>
<headline>Uzbekistan swings into $231 mln Jan-Sept trade gap.</headline>
<dateline>TASHKENT 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uzbekistan had a foreign trade deficit of $231 million in the first nine months of 1996 after a $319 million surplus in the same period last year, the State Statistics Committee said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>UZBEK FOREIGN TRADE (in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>			  Jan-Sep 96	 Jan-Sep 95</p>
<p>  Exports		 3,087		2,024</p>
<p>  Imports		 3,318		1,706</p>
<p>  Balance		  -231		 +319</p>
<p>NOTE - figures include trade between Uzbekistan and former Soviet republics in the Commonwealth of Independent States.</p>
<p>--Tashkent Newsroom +7 3712 361958</p>
</text>
